      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "> I cannot see any `maybe-uninitialized` warnings in CI logs, and this passes locally on aarch64.\n\nThis is interesting.\n\nThe CI job uses GCC 14.3:\n```\nC++ compiler .......................... GNU 14.3.0, /nix/store/wj1z9dwd3w62nfhvvla4bk1f3fq6mxi0-x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc-wrapper-14.3.0/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-g++\n```\n\nHowever, newer compilers still produce the `maybe-uninitialized` warning, as noted in https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35606#issuecomment-5130703059. For example:\n- on Fedora:\n```\nC++ compiler .......................... GNU 16.2.1, /bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32ucrt-g++\n```\n- on macOS + Homebrew:\n```\nC++ compiler .......................... GNU 16.2.0, /opt/homebrew/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-g++\n```\n\nACK 963f557a721b279a643db2982893c8aa667416c6 for our current CI job.",
